# Forum SSO local testing

The procedure lives in the README, section "Testando o SSO do fórum em localhost". Do not keep a second copy of the steps.

- `npm run dev:https` (`next dev --experimental-https`).
- On the forum origin: `localStorage.setItem('ifdb_dev_api_base', 'https://localhost:3000')`.
- Only `localhost` / `127.0.0.1` are accepted. Anything else falls through to production.
- The override covers mode 1 (the handshake) only. Mode 2 link interception, `collect.js`, and `tree-renderer.js` still hit production. Diagnose those against prod.
- A change under `.forum-frontend/` still has to be pasted into the forum's global JS by hand.
- `sso.js` state-machine checks can run with a fake `_userdata`, `sessionStorage`, and `fetch`, with no server.
- The local test writes the nonce to the real forum profile and uses the MongoDB in `.env`. `FORUM_ORIGIN` must match the forum Origin exactly, with no trailing slash.
